# Reduced TS, step 3a: relaxed surface scan along the forming bond (C8).
#
# Why a scan rather than OptTS: step 2 showed the frozen-core structure is an
# ORDER-3 SADDLE -- the relay mode (-799.57 cm-1, H135 + C129) plus an alpha-CH2
# ring mode (-261.87) and a mixed host mode (-52.52). The ring is strained
# because the reacting core is frozen at the r2SCAN-3c TS geometry while the host
# relaxed on the B97-3c surface. Handing that straight to OptTS means resolving
# three imaginary modes at once, and OptTS already failed once on this host.
#
# A relaxed scan varies one coordinate and re-optimizes everything else at each
# point, so the ring strain is resolved at every step and the maximum of the
# curve is a clean TS guess (ORCA manual 4.2: "The structure at the maximum of
# the curve is probably a very good guess for the true transition state").
#
# Coordinate: the forming bond O136...C129 -- 0-based 133 and 128 (0-based
# confirmed by the step-1 constraint echo: input 128 -> 1-based 129 = C129).
# Range 1.6 -> 2.8 A: the seed sits at 1.820, the r2SCAN-3c TS at 1.820 and the
# r2SCAN-3c product endpoint near 1.55, so the maximum lies inside this window.
#
# Next: from the scan maximum, an OptTS (inhess from a NumFreq at that point),
# or a direct NumFreq verdict if the maximum is already clean.
! QM/XTB B97-3c ddCOSMO(Water) Opt TightSCF

%QMMM
QMATOMS
	{61 64 120 121 122 124 125 126 128 129 130 131 132 133 134 135 136}
END
Charge_total 0
Mult_total 1
AutoFF_QM2_Method GFNFF
END

%geom
  Scan
    B 128 133 = 1.6, 2.8, 13
  end
  Calc_Hess true
  Recalc_Hess 50
end

%output jsonpropfile true end

%maxcore 4000

%pal
   nprocs 8
end

* xyzfile 0 1 job.xyz
